+# Level-4 Autonomy Flip Runbook (enable higher automation)
+
+This runbook describes steps, checks and rollback to flip the platform to a higher autonomy mode (e.g., from hybrid -> aggressive).
+
+Pre-reqs (must pass before flip)
+- All CI checks passing (quantize, canary, red-team).
+- DP per-token accounting validated in staging for at least 7 days.
+- Cosign KMS + OIDC approver mediator deployed and multisig test passed.
+- Retrain guard using Redis (HA) in place and cooldown/rate limits validated.
+- Prometheus/Grafana dashboards ready and alerting policies in place.
+
+Flip steps (operator)
+1. Notify stakeholders (Security/Legal/ML/Ops) and record consent in approvals log.
+2. Set a maintenance window and enable chat-on-call.
+3. Update OPA policy to new autonomy mode (example via gitops):
+   - git checkout infra/opa-policies
+   - edit policy: set autonomy_mode = "aggressive"
+   - git commit & push -> ArgoCD will apply
+4. Verify ArgoCD sync succeeded:
+   kubectl -n argocd get applications
+5. Trigger a dry-run canary:
+   argo submit --from workflowtemplate/lrm-canary-validate-gated -p candidate_image=<current_model_image> -p prometheus_url=http://prometheus.monitoring.svc:9090 -p max_blocked_incidents=1
+6. Watch the canary for 30 minutes and ensure:
+   - blocked incidents <= threshold
+   - P95 latency within SLO
+   - DP charges accounted and no failures
+
+If all pass, proceed:
+7. Switch OPA policy to risk-tolerant mapping (already versioned) and ensure orchestrator pulls it:
+   curl -X POST http://aegis-orchestrator.aegis-system.svc.cluster.local/reload_policies
+8. Record the flip in the evidence store: create cosign-signed note with who/when/why.
+
+Rollback steps (if any check fails)
+- Immediately set OPA policy back to previous autonomy_mode via git revert and ArgoCD sync.
+- Scale model-serving back to previous replicas:
+  kubectl -n model-serving scale deployment model-serving --replicas=2
+- If DP failures: set autonomy_mode to "conservative", notify billing and security, and open incident.
+- If safety regression: run auto-remediate workflow:
+  argo submit --from workflowtemplate/auto_remediate_retrain -p incident_id=<incident> || true
+
+Post-mortem & monitoring
+- Run full red-team suite and backtest historical incidents to compute false-auto rate.
+- Keep flip for at least 24h under elevated monitoring; collect metrics and sign-off for 7 days before further expansion.
+
